# "You can take this", said as LIGHT (docs/LOOK.md: the world is lit, not
# drawn). Whatever the `use` key would work right now lights up, in the colour
# of what it would do -- a cool catch for workable, a low warm one for the
# wrong tool in your hand, and almost nothing at all for something already
# picked over. No bracket, no ring, no mark on the glass.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/reach.tour --seed=7 --hour=21.5 --weather=clear:0
#
# Shot at dusk on purpose: this is exactly the hour a player is deciding what
# to gather before dark, and it is where light can say it and a mark cannot.
# The rule is Survival.use_target / Survival.describe_target and is not
# reimplemented anywhere in the lights system.
weather clear:0
zoom 7

hour 21.5
at prop:driftwood
wait 0.6
shot 01-workable-lights-up with prop:driftwood

# The same thing once it has been taken: the light goes with it.
press use 1.2
await took 3
wait 0.6
shot 02-and-goes-out-when-it-is-gone

# A thing the hand in the creel cannot work: lit, but low and warm, so the
# answer is "not with that" rather than "not at all".
at prop:stone
wait 0.6
shot 03-the-wrong-tool-reads-warm with prop:stone

# And by day it is still the answer, because it is a property of the thing and
# not of the dark.
hour 12
at prop:driftwood
wait 0.6
shot 04-by-day-as-well with prop:driftwood
